     bb    000 0 eng c  a(OCoLC)892343133  aGPObengerdacGPOdGPOdOCLCFdOINdGPOdLUEdFQGdOCLCAdOCLCQdOCLCOdGPO  apcc  an-us---aa------aa-cc---ap------  aGPOO  a1039-B (MF)0 aY 4.F 76/2:S.PRT.113-24zY 4.F 49:S.PRT.113-241 aUnited States.bCongress.bSenate.bCommittee on Foreign Relations,eauthor.0https://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n7800823010aRe-balancing the rebalance :bresourcing U.S. diplomatic strategy in the Asia-Pacific region : a majority staff report prepared for the use of the Committee on Foreign Relations, United States Senate, One Hundred Thirteenth Congress, second session, April 17, 2014. 1aWashington :bU.S. Government Printing Office,c2014.  a1 microfiche (v, 27 pages) :bnegative ;c11 x 15 cm.  atextbtxt2rdacontent  amicroformbh2rdamedia  amicrofichebhe2rdacarrier1 aS. Prt. / 113th Congress, 2d session ;v113-24  aPaper version available for sale by the Superintendent of Documents, U.S. Government Printing Office.  aShipping list no.: 2014-0209-M.  aIncludes bibliographical references.0 aLetter of transmittal. -- Executive summary. -- Recommendations. -- Development of the rebalance. -- Resourcing of the rebalance. -- China and the rebalance. -- Implementation of the rebalance. -- Acknowledgements.  aThis report by the majority staff of the Senate Foreign Relations Committee examines the progress made on the non-military elements of the Obama administration's policy to pursue a strategic rebalance towards the Asia-Pacific region. As this report finds, despite progress in some areas, implementation of the rebalance thus far has been uneven, which creates the risk that the rebalance may well end up as less than the sum of its parts. This report provides additional insight and perspective on the rebalance, and recommendations on how to properly resource and implement the rebalance to meet its strategic goals of enhancing prosperity, security, democratic values and human development in the Asia-Pacific region.10aUnited States.bDepartment of StatexAppropriations and expenditures.0https://id.loc.gov/authorities/subjects/sh85140832 0aUnited StatesxForeign relationszAsia. 0aUnited StatesxForeign relationszPacific Area. 0aUnited StatesxForeign relationszChina. 0aUnited StatesxForeign economic relationszAsia. 0aUnited StatesxForeign economic relationszPacific Area. 0aEconomic assistance, AmericanzAsia. 0aEconomic assistance, AmericanzPacific Area.17aUnited States.bDepartment of State.2fast0(OCoLC)fst01802976 7aDiplomatic relations.2fast0(OCoLC)fst01907412 7aEconomic assistance, American.2fast0(OCoLC)fst00901618 7aExpenditures, Public.2fast0(OCoLC)fst00918345 7aInternational economic relations.2fast0(OCoLC)fst00976891 7aAsia.2fast0(OCoLC)fst01240495 7aChina.2fast0(OCoLC)fst01206073 7aPacific Area.2fast0(OCoLC)fst01243504 7aUnited States.2fast0(OCoLC)fst01204155 4aLegislative materials. 7aLegislative materials.2fast0(OCoLC)fst01774285 7aLegislative materials.2lcgft0https://id.loc.gov/authorities/genreForms/gf201102636208iOnline version:aUnited States. Congress. Senate. Committee on Foreign Relations.tRe-balancing the rebalancew(OCoLC)87805334708iPrint version:aUnited States. Congress. Senate. Committee on Foreign Relations.tRe-balancing the rebalancew(OCoLC)879590758 0aS. prt. ;v113-24.0https://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n83707879  aC0bGPO  abca68 20141006b2014100602287cam a2200457Ii 00094669120261022142628.0150420s2015    mdua     bs  f000 0 eng d  a(OCoLC)907642910  aKSWbengerdacKSWdOCLCOdGPO  an-us---  aGPOO0 aHE 20.6234:1921 aBrown, Amy M.,cM.P.H.,eauthor.10aEmergency department visits and proximity to patients' residences, 2009-2010 /cAmy M. Brown ; Sandra L. Decker ; and Frederick W. Selck. 1aHyattsville, MD :bU.S. Department of Health and Human Services, Centers for Disease Control and Prevention, National Center for Heal