https://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/no200406632910aDefense acquisitions.pAssessments of major weapons programs :breport to Congressional Committees.1 aAssessments of major weapons programs1 iIssues for March 2005-March 2006 have title:aDefense acquisitions.pAssessments of selected major weapon programs1 iIssues for March 2007-March 2017 have title:aDefense acquisitions.pAssessments of selected weapon programs1 aAssessments of selected major weapon programs1 aAssessments of selected weapon programs 1aWashington, D.C. :bUnited States Government Accountability Office,c2003-2017.  a1 online resource (15 volumes) :bcolor illustrations  aAnnual  atextbtxt2rdacontent  acomputerbc2rdamedia  aonline resourcebcr2rdacarrier  atext filebPDF2rda1 aBegan with: May 2003; ceased with: March 2017.  aThis is GAO's annual assessment of DOD weapon system acquisitions, an area that is on GAO's High-Risk List. DOD and Congress have taken meaningful steps to improve the acquisition of major weapon systems, yet many programs are still falling short of cost and schedule estimates. Moreover, GAO has emphasized the importance of completing developmental testing before programs enter production and pointed out risks associated with such concurrent testing and production. With expected budgetary pressures, DOD cannot afford to miss opportunities to address inefficiencies in these programs to free up resources for higher priority needs.  aDescription based on: May 2003; title from PDF title page (GAO website, viewed April 21, 2020).  aLatest issue consulted: March 2017 (GAO website, viewed April 21, 2020).10aUnited States.bDepartment of DefensexProcurementvPeriodicals.17aUnited States.bDepartment of Defense.2fast0(OCoLC)fst01852447 0aWeapons systemszUnited StatesxDesign and constructionvPeriodicals. 0aUnited StatesxArmed ForcesxWeapons systemsxProcurementvPeriodicals. 7aArmed ForcesxProcurement.2fast0(OCoLC)fst00814624