 world to the modern world. The problems of training, logistics, tactics and strategy, and civil-military relations are remarkably consistent through time. This book features an international group of contributors, a consideration of major themes from ancient history to the modern world, and a look at the economic and social factors affecting warfare"--cProvided by publisher.  f© 2026 by Graham Wrightson, PhD, and Jerry W. Jones, PhDg2026 0aWarxHistory. 0aMilitary history.1 aWrightson, Grahamq(Graham Charles Liquorish),eeditor.1https://id.oclc.org/worldcat/entity/E39PCjFbWmc76MvQ8WdRcgjvjK1 aJones, Jerry W.,d1964-eeditor.1https://id.oclc.org/worldcat/entity/E39PCjtr9VpCwxmjXVrtXdYWrC2 aMarine Corps University (U.S.).bPress,eissuing body.08iOnline version:tMany faces of war & peace.dQuantico, Virginia : Marine Corps University Press, 2026w(OCoLC)1614950797  aC0bGPO  abc48 20261007  abc48 20260909  abc48 20260902  aBIBCONEWb20260406  aECIPb20260406  abc81 20260406b2026040603437cam a2200625 i 00147058520261007144728.0t|260304s2026    dcuab    b   f000 0 eng c  a2026006528  a9781959302254qpaperback  a1959302256  z9781959302254qpdf  a(OCoLC)1578840770  aDGPO/DLCbengerdacDLCdOCLCOdGPOdOCLCFdOCLCOdGPO  apcc  an-us-nc0http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/geographicAreas/n-us-nc  an-us-sc0http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/geographicAreas/n-us-sc  an-us-ga0http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/geographicAreas/n-us-ga  aGPOO00aE230.5.S7bS55 202600a973.33223/eng/202603100 aD 114.7/9:C 221 aSkinner, Harold Allen,cJr.,d1966-eauthor.4aut4http://id.loc.gov/vocabulary/relators/aut1https://id.oclc.org/worldcat/entity/E39PCjw4hQghbVMwyF6TPTjGf31http://id.loc.gov/rwo/agents/no201915593114aThe war in the Carolinas and Georgia, 1781-1782 /cby H. Allen Skinner. 1aWashington, D.C. :bCenter of Military History, United States Army,c2026.  a107 pages :billustrations (some color), maps (some color) ;c2