erior, Bureau of Land Management"--Cover of 1978-1979 issues.  aIssued in parts.  aIn scope of the U.S. Government Publishing Office Cataloging and Indexing Program (C&I) and Federal Depository Library Program (FDLP).  aThis is a publication issued by the United States federal government or produced with federal funds.  aA collection of work statements written by the various research units representing the Outer Continental Shelf Environmental Assessment Program. Each work statement describes the proposed research to be conducted on the environmental conditions of the Alaska continental shelf. The information includes the names the principal investigators, time and location of study, cost, research objective, strategy, analytical methods, information products, anticipated problems, management plan, and outlook. Some proposals include a bibliography. The Outer Continental Shelf Environmental Assessment Program (OCSEAP) was a part of the National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration (NOAA). The program was managed by NOAA under an interagency agreement with the Bureau of Land Management.  aAlso issued online.  aDescription based on: 1978 (October 1, 1977-September 30, 1978); title from title page.  aIssued as part of the Outer Continental Shelf Environmental Assessment Program.  aGPO Historic Shelflist Project- publication not in hand.20aOuter Continental Shelf Environmental Assessment Program.0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/names/n78063261 0aEnvironmental impact analysisxResearchzAlaska. 0aMarine mineral resourcesxResearchzAlaska. 0aOffshore oil well drillingxEnvironmental aspectsxResearchzAlaska. 0aOceanographyxResearchzAlaska. 0aContinental shelfxEnvironmental aspectszAlaska. 7aContinental shelfxEnvironmental aspects.2fast0(OCoLC)fst00876678 7aAlaska.2fast0(OCoLC)fst012044801https://id.oclc.org/worldcat/entity/E39QbtfRq9rTfb3H89Vvrr9x9c2 aEnvironmental Research Laboratories (U.S.)0http://id.loc.gov/authorities/n